CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*status)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct i2c_smbus_host_notify_status)...)
#180: FILE: drivers/i2c/i2c-core-smbus.c:781:
+	status = kzalloc(sizeof(struct i2c_smbus_host_notify_status),

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

